course: dictionary
lesson: 4831
title: One word, two jobs: husk
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A husk is the dry outer covering around some seeds and fruits. «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel.» Peel back means pull away, so the husk is the layer you pull off to reach the kernels inside.
explain: Husk can be a noun or a verb. Here it is a noun, a thing. In «To husk corn» it would be a verb, an action: to husk means to remove the husk. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. "Peel back the outer covering" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Clues also tell you what a husk is like. «A coconut is a seed in a fibrous, air-filled husk that floats and keeps sea water out.» Fibrous means made of threads, and air-filled means it has air inside. Those clues explain why a coconut can float.
explain: Sometimes a word has a figurative meaning. «A husk of his former self» does not mean a dry seed. Former means before, so the phrase means someone who has become weak and empty, like a dry shell with nothing left inside.
fact: A husk is the dry outer covering of some seeds or fruits, such as corn, coconuts and rice.
fact: A husk can also be the dry, empty shell of something when the inside has gone.
fact: To husk means to remove the husk, as when you husk corn.
fact: «Husky» is a different word that can describe a rough, deep voice.
fact: A coconut's husk is fibrous and air-filled, so the coconut can float for months and keep sea water out.
exercise: «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel.» What is the husk in this sentence? | *The dry outer covering around the corn | A kernel inside the corn | A long silky thread | A green leaf on a plant
exercise: «A coconut is a seed in a fibrous, air-filled husk that floats and keeps sea water out.» What does fibrous mean? | Sweet to taste | *Made of threads | Very heavy and hard | Frozen solid
exercise: «Pau Amma's shell falls off like a husk off a coconut.» What does this suggest? | Something wet and sticky grows bigger | Something is cooked and eaten | *Something dry and empty falls away | Something is painted bright red
test: «A husk of his former self» means what? | Someone who has just finished a big meal | Someone who speaks in a deep, rough voice | *Someone who has become weak and empty, like a dry shell | Someone who is very tall and strong
test: Which phrase means the same as "to husk"? | To sweep the kitchen floor | To float across the sea | *To remove the husk | To grow a new seed
exam: «A coconut can float for months and travel thousands of kilometres across the sea and still sprout.» Why can the husk help it travel? | It is so heavy that it sinks to the bottom | *It is fibrous and air-filled, so it floats and keeps sea water out | It is sweet, so fish follow it across the sea | It melts in salt water and lets the seed out
